archive-retention.instructions:
# Archive retention

The records office keeps:

- signed maps for 36 months;
- unsigned maps for 14 months;
- calendars for 5 months;
- ledgers for 84 months.

Signed status changes the period only for maps. A record under legal hold is kept until the hold is lifted: report its retention as "hold" instead of a number of months. Laboratory records are not kept by the records office.

specimen-log-retention.instructions:
# Specimen log retention

The laboratory keeps:

- specimen logs for 30 months, or 60 months when the specimen was sent out for external testing;
- bench sheets for 9 months, or 18 months when a bench sheet records a failed control;
- instrument printouts for 3 months.

Records-office documents follow the archive retention guide instead.
